  ],
  "contract": "utimensat(2) and utime(2): tv_sec is a calendar time and may be negative, and Linux stores a pre-Epoch time on filesystems whose timestamp range allows it (tmpfs and overlayfs in the saved runs).",
  "observed": "By source reading at the pin (not run): futimens and utimes with tv_sec = -1 fail with EINVAL.",
